`tokens` prints one file's token stream, one token per line as
`line:col kind lexeme`. It is a debugging aid for the lexer itself, and
it is now something you have to ask for by name: it was `hllc`'s
default mode until #129, which is why a seven-line file greeting a new
user with twenty-one lines of token dump was the first thing #88
listed.

`errors.trycmd` pins what a lexer error looks like on this path. What
this transcript holds is the successful shape — that a token carries a
position, a kind, and the exact source text it came from.

```console
$ hllc tokens web.hll
1:1 Ident "service"
1:9 Ident "web"
1:13 LBrace "{"
2:3 Ident "image"
2:9 Str "nginx:alpine"
3:1 RBrace "}"
4:1 Eof ""

```
